cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software in research or teaching, please cite it as below."
title: "Laplace Demon: an honest predictor laboratory for finite universes"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "madnessbrainsbl"
repository-code: "https://github.com/madnessbrainsbl/Laplace_Demon"
url: "https://github.com/madnessbrainsbl/Laplace_Demon"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.1
date-released: "2026-09-22"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free desktop laboratory that executes the Laplace's demon
  thought experiment: exact finite-model prediction and predecessor enumeration,
  law inference from observed events, numerical sensitivity diagnostics,
  a quantum kernel with decoherence and a CHSH calculation, the
  information-theoretic Laplace coefficient L = I(E;K)/H(E), active-inference
  knowledge foraging, and finite illustrations of physical and logical limits.
  These models do not prove universal physical impossibility or computational
  irreducibility. Includes a deterministic cellular prediction game.
keywords:
  - laplace-demon
  - determinism
  - cellular-automata
  - information-theory
  - quantum-mechanics
  - bell-inequality
  - chaos-theory
  - active-inference
  - thermodynamics-of-information
  - philosophy-of-science
